{"type":"new","contents":"/-\nInfoGeometry/OperatorAlgebra/RealGWClifford.lean\n\nReal Garding-Wightman Clifford module splitting.\n\nTheorem-safe formalization inspired by:\n\n  Esther Galina, Aroldo Kaplan, Linda Saal,\n  \"Split Clifford Modules over a Hilbert Space\",\n  arXiv:math/0204117v3.\n\nThis file keeps the owner lane real.\n\nIt does not assert that every complex/GW/CAR module has a real form.  It\nrecords the certificate-gated splitting criterion:\n\n  reflected measure equivalent to the original measure,\n  complement-invariant multiplicity,\n  measurable real-structure field r(x),\n  r(x) r(1-x) = 1,\n  r(x) c_k(1-x) = (-1)^k c_k(x) r(x + delta_k).\n\nIt also does not identify this real Clifford module lane with split `Cl(n,n)`,\n`O(n,n)`, or `Pin(n,n)` data.  That requires a separate doubled Krein /\nsplit-quadratic certificate.\n-/\n\nimport Mathlib\n\nnoncomputable section\n\nnamespace InfoGeometry.OperatorAlgebra.RealGWClifford\n\n/--\nReal Clifford Hilbert module data.\n\nThis is the real owner object: a real Hilbert carrier with Clifford generators\nrepresented by real operators.\n\nThe intended relation is:\n\n  J z * J w + J w * J z = -2 <z,w> 1,\n\nand in an orthonormal sequence:\n\n  J_i^2 = -1,\n  J_i J_j = -J_j J_i  for i != j.\n\nThe actual analytic Hilbert/skew-adjoint structure is certificate-gated.\n-/\nstructure RealCliffordHilbertModuleData where\n  /-- Real generator Hilbert space `Z`. -/\n  GeneratorSpace : Type\n\n  /-- Real module Hilbert carrier `H`. -/\n  HilbertCarrier : Type\n\n  /-- Real operator carrier on `H`. -/\n  OperatorCarrier : Type\n\n  /-- Clifford action `Z -> End_R(H)`. -/\n  cliffordAction : GeneratorSpace -> OperatorCarrier\n\n  /-- Distinguished countable generator labels, if using a sequence. -/\n  GeneratorIndex : Type\n\n  /-- Sequence of real Clifford generators `J_i`. -/\n  J : GeneratorIndex -> OperatorCarrier\n\n  /-- Certificate that the `J_i` are real-linear operators. -/\n  realLinearityCertificate : Type\n\n  /-- Certificate that each generator is skew-adjoint. -/\n  skewAdjointCertificate : Type\n\n  /-- Certificate that each `J_i^2 = -1`. -/\n  squareMinusOneCertificate : Type\n\n  /-- Certificate that distinct generators anticommute. -/\n  anticommutationCertificate : Type\n\n  /-- Certificate that the action satisfies the Clifford relation. -/\n  cliffordRelationCertificate : Type\n\n  /-- Guard: no complex scalar field is the owner of this data record. -/\n  realOnlyCertificate : Type\n\n/--\nGarding-Wightman occupation-space data.\n\nThis records the measure/fiber/cocycle surface used to classify CAR/Clifford\nmodules.\n\nThe data record is intentionally abstract: it does not construct measure theory or\ndirect integrals.  It stores exactly the data whose analytic realization is\nneeded for the Galina-Kaplan-Saal splitting criterion.\n-/\nstructure GWOccupationData where\n  /-- Occupation-number space, morally `{0,1}^N`. -/\n  OccupationSpace : Type\n\n  /-- Finite-flip group, morally `Delta`. -/\n  FiniteFlipGroup : Type\n\n  /-- Distinguished flips `delta_k`. -/\n  FlipIndex : Type\n\n  /-- Action `x + delta`. -/\n  flipAction : OccupationSpace -> FiniteFlipGroup -> OccupationSpace\n\n  /-- Distinguished single-coordinate flip. -/\n  delta : FlipIndex -> FiniteFlipGroup\n\n  /-- Complement operation `x |-> 1 - x`. -/\n  complement : OccupationSpace -> OccupationSpace\n\n  /-- Measure data `mu`. -/\n  measureData : Type\n\n  /-- Reflected measure data, morally `mu_tilde(E)=mu(1-E)`. -/\n  reflectedMeasureData : Type\n\n  /-- Multiplicity function/fiber dimension data `nu`. -/\n  multiplicityData : Type\n\n  /-- Direct-integral fiber data `H_x`. -/\n  fiberData : Type\n\n  /-- Clifford/GW cocycle operators `c_k(x)`. -/\n  cocycleOperatorData : Type\n\n  /-- Certificate that `mu` is quasi-invariant under finite flips. -/\n  finiteFlipQuasiInvarianceCertificate : Type\n\n  /-- Certificate that the `c_k` satisfy the GW cocycle equations. -/\n  ckCocycleCertificate : Type\n\n/--\nReal splitting certificate for a GW module.\n\nThis is the theorem-safe content of the Galina-Kaplan-Saal real-form\ncriterion.  A real form exists only after all of these certificates are supplied.\n-/\nstructure GWRealSplittingCertificate where\n  /-- Underlying GW occupation data record. -/\n  gw : GWOccupationData\n\n  /-- Certificate that reflected measure and original measure are equivalent. -/\n  measureReflectionEquivalenceCertificate : Type\n\n  /-- Certificate that multiplicity is complement-invariant: `nu(x)=nu(1-x)` a.e. -/\n  multiplicityComplementInvariantCertificate : Type\n\n  /-- Measurable family `r(x): H_x -> H_{1-x}`. -/\n  realStructureField : Type\n\n  /-- Certificate that `r(x)` is antilinear in the auxiliary complexified model. -/\n  antilinearCertificate : Type\n\n  /-- Certificate that `r(x)` preserves the fiber norm. -/\n  normPreservingCertificate : Type\n\n  /-- Certificate that `r(x) r(1-x)=1`. -/\n  involutionCertificate : Type\n\n  /--\n  Certificate of the key compatibility:\n\n    r(x) c_k(1-x) = (-1)^k c_k(x) r(x+delta_k).\n  -/\n  ckRealCompatibilityCertificate : Type\n\n  /-- Measurability certificate for the field `r(x)`. -/\n  measurabilityCertificate : Type\n\n  /-- Resulting invariant real form. -/\n  invariantRealForm : Type\n\n  /-- Guard: real splitting is not automatic for GW/CAR modules. -/\n  noAutomaticRealSplitCertificate : Type\n\n/--\nThe theorem-safe owner target:\n\na GW module has a real splitting only if a `GWRealSplittingCertificate` is supplied.\n-/\ndef GWRealSplittingTarget : Prop :=\n  Nonempty GWRealSplittingCertificate\n\n/-- Construct the GW real-splitting target from explicit certificate data. -/\ntheorem constructGWRealSplittingTarget\n    (W : GWRealSplittingCertificate) :\n    GWRealSplittingTarget := by\n  exact ⟨W⟩\n\nnamespace GWRealSplittingCertificate\n\n/-- The measure-reflection equivalence certificate is exposed as an accessor. -/\ndef measureReflectionGuard\n    (W : GWRealSplittingCertificate) : Type :=\n  W.measureReflectionEquivalenceCertificate\n\n@[simp] theorem measureReflectionGuard_eq\n    (W : GWRealSplittingCertificate) :\n    W.measureReflectionGuard = W.measureReflectionEquivalenceCertificate :=\n  rfl\n\n/-- The multiplicity complement-invariance certificate is exposed as an accessor. -/\ndef multiplicityComplementGuard\n    (W : GWRealSplittingCertificate) : Type :=\n  W.multiplicityComplementInvariantCertificate\n\n@[simp] theorem multiplicityComplementGuard_eq\n    (W : GWRealSplittingCertificate) :\n    W.multiplicityComplementGuard =\n      W.multiplicityComplementInvariantCertificate :=\n  rfl\n\n/-- The `r(x) r(1-x)=1` certificate is exposed as an accessor. -/\ndef realStructureInvolutionGuard\n    (W : GWRealSplittingCertificate) : Type :=\n  W.involutionCertificate\n\n@[simp] theorem realStructureInvolutionGuard_eq\n    (W : GWRealSplittingCertificate) :\n    W.realStructureInvolutionGuard = W.involutionCertificate :=\n  rfl\n\n/-- The `r c_k` compatibility certificate is exposed as an accessor. -/\ndef ckRealCompatibilityGuard\n    (W : GWRealSplittingCertificate) : Type :=\n  W.ckRealCompatibilityCertificate\n\n@[simp] theorem ckRealCompatibilityGuard_eq\n    (W : GWRealSplittingCertificate) :\n    W.ckRealCompatibilityGuard = W.ckRealCompatibilityCertificate :=\n  rfl\n\n/-- Real splitting is explicitly non-automatic. -/\ndef realSplitAutomaticityGuard\n    (W : GWRealSplittingCertificate) : Type :=\n  W.noAutomaticRealSplitCertificate\n\n@[simp] theorem realSplitAutomaticityGuard_eq\n    (W : GWRealSplittingCertificate) :\n    W.realSplitAutomaticityGuard = W.noAutomaticRealSplitCertificate :=\n  rfl\n\nend GWRealSplittingCertificate\n\n/--\nFinite-dimensional Cartan-Killing splitting data.\n\nThe paper recalls the classical finite-dimensional condition: complex Clifford\nmodules split over `R` exactly in specific mod-4 cases.  This data record stores\nthat as theorem-bank certificate data, not as an automatic theorem of arbitrary\nfinite data.\n-/\nstructure FiniteRealCliffordSplittingData where\n  /-- Finite generator dimension `m`. -/\n  generatorDimension : Nat\n\n  /-- Mod-4 residue data. -/\n  modFourResidueData : Type\n\n  /-- Certificate that the Cartan-Killing finite splitting criterion applies. -/\n  finiteSplittingCriterionCertificate : Type\n\n  /-- Guard: finite-dimensional residue does not control infinite GW splitting. -/\n  noFiniteToInfiniteAutomaticityCertificate : Type\n\n/--\nFermi-Fock non-splitting guard data.\n\nThe paper notes that the basic Fermi-Fock representation is irreducible over\n`R` and does not split in the infinite-dimensional setting.  This data record\nrecords that as a guard against treating CAR/Fock data as automatically\nreal-split.\n-/\nstructure FermiFockRealSplitGuardData where\n  /-- Fermi-Fock representation data. -/\n  fermiFockRepresentation : Type\n\n  /-- Certificate that the measure is discrete/supported on one finite-flip orbit. -/\n  discreteOrbitMeasureCertificate : Type\n\n  /-- Certificate that reflected measure equivalence fails. -/\n  reflectedMeasureFailureCertificate : Type\n\n  /-- Certificate that no invariant real form is obtained in this model. -/\n  noInvariantRealFormCertificate : Type\n\n  /-- Guard: Fermi-Fock does not supply the real split owner lane. -/\n  noFermiFockAutomaticRealSplitCertificate : Type\n\n/--\nComparison to the split doubled-Krein lane.\n\nThe Galina-Kaplan-Saal theorem supplies real Clifford module splitting data.\nIt does not automatically supply split `Cl(n,n)`, `O(n,n)`, or `Pin(n,n)`\ndata.\n\nThose require a doubled Krein / split-quadratic certificate.\n-/\nstructure RealGWToSplitKreinComparisonData where\n  /-- Real Clifford Hilbert module. -/\n  realCliffordModule : RealCliffordHilbertModuleData\n\n  /-- Optional GW real splitting certificate. -/\n  gwRealSplitting : GWRealSplittingCertificate\n\n  /-- Doubled Krein carrier data. -/\n  doubledKreinCarrier : Type\n\n  /-- Split quadratic form / signature `(n,n)` certificate. -/\n  splitQuadraticCertificate : Type\n\n  /-- Real split Clifford algebra `Cl(n,n)` certificate. -/\n  clnnCertificate : Type\n\n  /-- Full `O(n,n)` symmetry certificate. -/\n  fullONNCertificate : Type\n\n  /-- `Pin(n,n)` reflection/CPT certificate. -/\n  pinNNCPTCertificate : Type\n\n  /--\n  Guard: real Clifford splitting from GW theory is not automatically the same\n  as split `Cl(n,n)` / `O(n,n)` / `Pin(n,n)` data.\n  -/\n  noAutomaticSplitKreinCertificate : Type\n\n/-- Owner target for a supplied comparison from real GW data to split Krein data. -/\ndef RealGWToSplitKreinComparisonTarget : Prop :=\n  Nonempty RealGWToSplitKreinComparisonData\n\n/-- Construct the split-Krein comparison target from explicit certificate data. -/\ntheorem constructRealGWToSplitKreinComparisonTarget\n    (P : RealGWToSplitKreinComparisonData) :\n    RealGWToSplitKreinComparisonTarget := by\n  exact ⟨P⟩\n\nend InfoGeometry.OperatorAlgebra.RealGWClifford\n\n","mtime":1778318490435}